# Lock-in coaching: minimize full Gemini vision

Full-desktop screenshot → Gemini vision is expensive (tokens + free-tier RPD). Prefer cheaper signals first.

## Preference order (use in this order)

1. **Local OS events** (free): frontmost app switch, window title, browser URL/tabs — instant hard nags for Discord, Instagram, shopping, email, texting.
2. **Local OCR** (Apple Vision `.fast` on a small focused-window JPEG): read the webpage pixels when URL automation fails; label YouTube/Instagram/etc from text.
3. **Local quantized text model** (Ollama `qwen2.5:0.5b`): title/URL/OCR excerpt → on-task JSON.
4. **Local tiny VLM** (Ollama `moondream`, rare ~45s): only when OCR/OS still look unclear.
5. **Gemini text** only if local models are down or low-confidence.
6. **Full-desktop Gemini vision** (last resort): sparse. Skip while already distracted locally.

## Do / don't

- **Do** interrupt on app/tab open/switch without waiting for vision.
- **Do** treat YouTube as contextual (study vs entertainment) via text, not “any YouTube = bad”.
- **Don't** add new frequent `grab_desktop_jpeg` / `analyze_session` loops.
- **Don't** retry failed vision calls aggressively — that burns daily quota.
- **Don't** send screenshots when URL/title/page text is enough to decide.
